WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.207
Services sell better when packaged as outcomes, not vague hourly fog.

00:00:04.207 --> 00:00:06.501
This lesson is about service packaging.

00:00:06.501 --> 00:00:08.031
Hours, outcomes, async options.

00:00:08.031 --> 00:00:10.708
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:10.708 --> 00:00:14.532
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:14.532 --> 00:00:20.268
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:20.268 --> 00:00:24.475
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:24.475 --> 00:00:29.064
Stay practical: package a service v1 before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:29.384 --> 00:00:35.708
Package service version one with hours or milestones, the outcome, and async options if you use them.

00:00:35.708 --> 00:00:38.312
Remember the objective: package a service v1.

00:00:38.312 --> 00:00:42.404
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:42.404 --> 00:00:46.868
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:46.868 --> 00:00:50.960
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:55.424
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:55.744 --> 00:00:59.147
Bound the work: start, done, and what happens between.

